                        Hook Reference
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
                        Each hook runs in a sandboxed Lua 5.4 environment with access to the request context and built-in modules.
                    </p>

                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                        <!-- on_request -->
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:bg-white/[0.03] transition-all">
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 flex items-center justify-center">
                                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"/></svg>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="font-bold text-white font-mono text-sm">on_request</h3>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Pre-routing</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">Authentication, WAF rules, request validation. Runs before the target backend is resolved.</p>
                            <div class="rounded-lg bg-black/30 border border-white/5 p-3">
                                <code class="text-xs text-gray-300 leading-relaxed block">
                                    <span class="tk">function</span> <span class="tf">on_request</span>(<span class="tt">req</span>)<br>
                                    &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tc">-- inspect req:method(), req:path()</span><br>
                                    &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tc">-- inspect req:header("Authorization")</span><br>
                                    &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tk">return</span> req:<span class="tf">deny</span>(<span class="tn">403</span>, <span class="ts">"Forbidden"</span>)<br>
                                    <span class="tk">end</span>
                                </code>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- on_route -->
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:bg-white/[0.03] transition-all">
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 flex items-center justify-center">
                                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-cyan-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6"/></svg>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="font-bold text-white font-mono text-sm">on_route</h3>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Routing override</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">Dynamic routing, A/B testing, canary deploys. Return a URL string to override the resolved target.</p>
                            <div class="rounded-lg bg-black/30 border border-white/5 p-3">
                                <code class="text-xs text-gray-300 leading-relaxed block">
                                    <span class="tk">function</span> <span class="tf">on_route</span>(<span class="tt">req</span>, <span class="tt">target</span>)<br>
                                    &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tc">-- return URL string to override</span><br>
                                    &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tk">return</span> <span class="ts">"http://canary:8081"</span><br>
                                    <span class="tk">end</span>
                                </code>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- on_response -->
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:bg-white/[0.03] transition-all">
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-teal-500/10 flex items-center justify-center">
                                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-teal-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M7 16V4m0 0L3 8m4-4l4 4m6 0v12m0 0l4-4m-4 4l-4-4"/></svg>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="font-bold text-white font-mono text-sm">on_response</h3>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Post-backend</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">CORS headers, header stripping, body transforms. Modify the response before it reaches the client.</p>
                            <div class="rounded-lg bg-black/30 border border-white/5 p-3">
                                <code class="text-xs text-gray-300 leading-relaxed block">
                                    <span class="tc">-- Available methods:</span><br>
                                    resp:<span class="tf">set_header</span>(<span class="ts">"X-Key"</span>, <span class="ts">"val"</span>)<br>
                                    resp:<span class="tf">remove_header</span>(<span class="ts">"Server"</span>)<br>
                                    resp:<span class="tf">set_status</span>(<span class="tn">200</span>)<br>
                                    resp:<span class="tf">replace_body</span>(<span class="ts">"new body"</span>)
                                </code>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- on_request_end -->
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-900 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:bg-white/[0.03] transition-all">
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-orange-500/10 flex items-center justify-center">
                                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-orange-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 17v-2m3 2v-4m3 4v-6m2 10H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z"/></svg>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="font-bold text-white font-mono text-sm">on_request_end</h3>
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Fire-and-forget</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">Logging, metrics collection, analytics. Receives <code class="text-orange-300 text-xs bg-orange-500/10 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">duration_ms</code> and <code class="text-orange-300 text-xs bg-orange-500/10 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">target_url</code>. Cannot modify the response.</p>
                            <div class="rounded-lg bg-black/30 border border-white/5 p-3">
                                <code class="text-xs text-gray-300 leading-relaxed block">
                                    <span class="tk">function</span> <span class="tf">on_request_end</span>(<span class="tt">req</span>, <span class="tt">resp</span>,<br>
                                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tt">duration_ms</span>, <span class="tt">target_url</span>)<br>
                                    &nbsp;&nbsp;log.<span class="tf">info</span>(<span class="ts">"Took "</span> .. duration_ms .. <span class="ts">"ms"</span>)<br>
                                    <span class="tk">end</span>
                                </code>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

